So gamepad doesn't auto-join a slot; it just gives input for human slots. The claim "PAD Any gamepad auto-joins" in the select screen tip is misleading. We should either implement auto-join or adjust the text. Implementing: when a gamepad connects, if there's a free/off slot, set it to human so the pad can control it. But mapping pad index to slot: InputManager.stateFor(slot) finds `pads.find(p => p.index === slot)`. If gamepad index 0 controls slot 0; index 1 slot 1. On gamepadconnected, if slot index exists and is off, set that slot to human and rerender if on select screen. But if slot is CPU, should it replace CPU? "auto-joins" implies yes maybe. However, we don't want to disrupt an active battle. The event during battle could add a human mid-match? Not supported by game. Better make the tip accurate: "PAD Connects to any human slot" or "PAD Auto-joins on select". Alternatively implement auto-join when on select screen:
```
window.addEventListener('gamepadconnected', e => {
  const idx = e.gamepad.index;
  if (idx > 3) return;
  if (this.screen === 'select') {
    const slot = this.config.slots[idx];
    if (slot.type === 'off') { slot.type='human'; ... }
  }
  toast(...)
});
```
But the user still has to open custom match to use it, and Quick Play doesn't allow P2 gamepad unless slot1 is human (it's CPU). Quick Play is 1v1 vs CPU; gamepad index 0 can control P1 human. That's fine.

To keep promises true, update the tip to "PAD Connects to P1-P4" and not claim auto-join. Or implement a small auto-join in select. The requirement says support gamepads, not auto-join. Let's change the text to "PAD Auto-detected · joins a human slot" maybe. But that still suggests. Simpler: "PAD Connects to P1-P4". This is accurate: gamepads with index 0-3 control the corresponding slot if it's human.

But how does a gamepad control P1 if index 1? stateFor(0) finds p.index===0. Slots are tied to pad indices. Fine.

Also the title "Any gamepad auto-joins" was in the lineup tip. Let's update to "PAD DETECTED · TAKES ITS SLOT". Hmm. Keep concise:
`<span class="tip-key">PAD</span> Gamepads control P1–P4`
This is accurate. Do it.

