But on iPhone in portrait, safe-area-inset-top is ~47px; adding it to `.hud-topline` top 8+47=55 and cards 46+47=93. System buttons 8+47=55. Then topline at 55..75 and system buttons at 55..91 → overlap horizontally on narrow. The 560 rule moves topline to 52+47=99, cards 88+47=135. Fine. But the mobile 760 rule sets topline top 8+47=55, cards 46+47=93; at widths 561-760 there's no collision with buttons horizontally as computed. Fine.

But `.screen` padding top adds 47 on mobile portrait, shifting title content down 47. On iPhone with browser chrome, the visual viewport may already exclude the notch; env(safe-area-inset-top) is nonzero only in fullscreen/standalone or with viewport-fit=cover, which we have. Adding is correct.

However, `env(safe-area-inset-top)` on iOS Safari when not fullscreen is usually 0 for the top (browser chrome), but in standalone PWA it's 47. Fine.

The `.screen` animation uses transform; no issue.

